<br/>\n<span class=\"strong\">Diving Instructor</span>: Try both! When you are set up with the correct equipment and training, they are both safe and enjoyable activities. Do you like to go swimming in the ocean?<br/><span class=\"strong prelo-dialogue-110\">John</span>: For sure.", "time": "3000"}, {"image": "engenn4le12ob01re2img02.jpg", "id": 3, "text": "<span class=\"strong prelo-dialogue-110\">Diving Instructor</span>: Then go diving. You should go for a dive in the feeding areas off the Baja Peninsula. Those are the best places to see manta rays and sharks.<br/>\n<span class=\"strong\">John</span>: What? Sharks?", "time": "17400"}, {"image": "engenn4le12ob01re2img03.jpg", "id": 4, "text": "<span class=\"strong prelo-dialogue-110\">Diving Instructor</span>:  Don't worry, there's no danger. Sharks don't attack humans. Use good diving equipment and take a lesson with one of our excellent instructors. Don't forget to bring an underwater camera! You could go snorkeling in the afternoon.<br/>\n<span class=\"strong\">John</span>: Sounds cool!", "time": "28200"}], "coverimg": "engenn4le12ob01re2img01.jpg"}, "type": "slideshow"}], "template_override": 1, "_data": [], "type": "audio", "title": ""}], "id": 0, "type": "scholar", "_data": [{"type": "lab_options", "contents": [{"content": true, "type": "has_nav"}, {"content": true, "type": "has_exercise_controls"}]}]}]}